    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situated on a quiet cul de sac at this well known, mature, and popular residential area, this home is close to all amenities of Dungarvan town, and a short walking distance to Dungarvan Business and Industrial Estate. An extension was added to the rear of the house some years ago, incorporating a conservatory from the kitchen/dining area, and a substantial addition to the garage, which presents huge potential to convert this space into living accommodation and a downstairs bedroom.\r\nThis house has an ideal aspect with a private sunny south west rear garden with direct access through sliding doors from the conservatory, and spacious front garden with off street parking for two cars.\r\nThis home presents a great opportunity to acquire a house with huge potential at this most desirable and mature area of Dungarvan town.\r\n\r\nViewing Strictly by Appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor: \r\n\r\nEntrance Hall:\t 4.2m x 1.8m (13' 9\" x 5' 9\") \r\nThe large bright spacious hallway creates a welcoming atmosphere to the home boasting carpet flooring, solid timber stairs with carpet covering, 3- point centre light, phone point.\r\n\r\nSitting Room: \t4.3m x 3.4m (14' 1\" x 11' 0\") \r\nCarpet floor covering, roller window blinds, curtains, 5-point centre light fitting, TV point. \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining: \t5.2m x 3.3m (17' 0\" x 10' 8\")\r\nSolid timber fitted kitchen, cooker, dishwasher, fridge-freezer, extractor fan, solid fuel stove, double doors with glass panels to conservatory. \r\n\r\nHotpress: \r\nImmersion water heater and storage. \r\n\r\nConservatory:\t 4m x 2.2m (13' 1\" x 7' 2\")\r\nCeramic floor tiles, double sliding doors to south side sunny patio area, roller window blinds. Private rear garden. \r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor: \r\n\r\nLanding:\t\t 2.3m x 1.9m (7' 5\" x 6' 2\")\r\nWith carpet flooring, centre lighting, stira stairs to attic space, smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1: \t\t6m x 2.8m (19' 6\" x 9' 2\")\r\nCarpet floor covering, curtains, roller window blinds, built-in wardrobes, centre lighting. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2: \t\t3.4m x 3m (11' 1\" x 9' 8\")\r\nCarpet floor covering, curtains, roller window blinds, built-in wardrobes and vanity unit.  \r\n\r\nBedroom 3: \t\t3.4m x 2.2m (11' 1\" x 7' 2\")\r\nCarpet floor covering, built-in wardrobes, curtain, centre light. \r\n\r\nBathroom: \t\t2m x 1.3m (6' 5\" x 4' 3\") \r\nWC, whb, double shower unit with sliding door and power shower fitting, ceramic floor tiles, ceramic wall tiles, centre lighting.\r\n\r\nGarage/Workshop:  12.2m x 3.5 (40’ 0” x 11’5”)\r\nLarge space suitable for conversion to living space and/or/downstairs, bedroom plumbed for washing machine/dryer, oil fired boiler, solid timber double doors to the front."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Outside:\r\n\r\n•\tSituated at a great location in Dungarvan town.\r\n•\tWalking distance to Dungarvan Industrial Estate.\r\n•\tWalking distance to all town amenities.\r\n•\tClose to schools and leisure amenities.\r\n•\tFront and rear gardens.\r\n•\tSunny and private walled rear garden.\r\n•\tSouth side and private patio area off the conservatory.\r\n•\tFront garden with parking for two cars.\r\n\r\n\t\t\r\nIncluded :\r\n\r\n•\tLight fittings.\r\n•\tFloor coverings.\r\n•\tFixtures and fittings.                                                                                           \r\n\r\nGeneral features;\r\n\r\n•\tSpacious accommodation throughout.\r\n•\tExtension of conservatory at the rear of the house.\r\n•\tAttached garage and workshop …. All accessible from the house.\r\n•\tExtension to the garage ……. Ideal for conversion to living space.\r\n•\tWalled rear garden.\r\n•\tOil fired central heating.\r\n•\tPVC double glazed windows.\r\n•\tPVC facia and soffit.\r\n•\tClose access to the N25 Waterford/Cork route.\r\n•\tCable TV and broadband.\r\n•\tExcellent location…..close to schools and all town amenities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: E1"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "From Grattan Square proceed along Mary Street and turn right at the Parish Church, follow this road past the Garda Station until the turn off right before the Circle-K garage, turn an immediate right into Western Bay, along this road for 50 meters and turn right into the cul de sac, see No. 21 Western Bay on the right side, see the Morrissey Properties sign at the front of the property.\r\n___________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n\r\nNOTE.\r\n\r\nDNG Morrissey properties, for themselves and for the Vendors or Lessors of the property whose Agents they are, give notice that; 1. The particulars contained herein are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or tenants, and do not constitute any part of any offer or contract and are not in any way legally binding. 2. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. 3. No person in the employment of DNG Morrissey Properties has the authority to make or give representation or warranty whatever in relation to this development. 4. The particulars contained herein are confidential and are given on the strict understanding that all negotiations shall be conducted through DNG Morrissey Properties. 5. DNG Morrissey Properties disclaims all liability and responsibility for any direct and/or indirect loss or damage which may be suffered by any recipient through relying on any particular contained in or omitted from the aforementioned particulars.\r\n\r\n\r\n___________________________________________________________________________"
